    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">01. Overview</span>

        <h2>Project Overview</h2>

        <p>
            This project involved the development of a SAP CPI integration to
            replicate organizational Foundation Objects into SAP SuccessFactors
            Employee Central.
        </p>

        <p>
            The integration processes several organizational objects, including
            Business Units, Divisions, Departments, Units, Teams and Cost Centers.
        </p>

        <p>
            SAP CPI receives an encrypted file through SFTP containing the
            organizational structure and processes it through a scheduled nightly
            execution.
        </p>

        <p>
            The integration supports both Delta Load and Full Load processing
            modes and includes additional logic for dependency management,
            effective-dated processing and execution reporting.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">02. Architecture</span>

        <h2>Integration Architecture</h2>

        <p>
            SAP CPI acts as the processing and orchestration layer responsible
            for receiving, decrypting, validating and synchronizing organizational
            data with SAP SuccessFactors Employee Central.
        </p>

        <p>
            The encrypted file is received through SFTP. SAP CPI decrypts the
            file, reads the organizational records and applies the required
            processing logic before communicating with SuccessFactors through
            OData APIs.
        </p>

        <p>
            At the end of the execution, CPI generates a processing report
            containing the result of the processed records.
        </p>

        <div class="architecture-flow">

            <div class="architecture-item">
                <h3>SFTP</h3>
                <p>Encrypted Organizational File</p>
            </div>

            <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

            <div class="architecture-item">
                <h3>SAP CPI</h3>
                <p>
                    Decryption · Filtering · Dependency Management · Validation
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

            <div class="architecture-item">
                <h3>SAP SuccessFactors EC</h3>
                <p>Foundation Object OData Processing</p>
            </div>

            <div class="architecture-arrow">↓</div>

            <div class="architecture-item">
                <h3>SAP CPI</h3>
                <p>Execution Report · Success / Error Details</p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">03. Foundation Object Scope</span>

        <h2>Organizational Data Replication</h2>

        <p>
            The integration supports the replication of the Foundation Objects
            required to maintain the organizational structure in SAP SuccessFactors
            Employee Central.
        </p>

        <p>The objects processed include:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Business Unit</li>
            <li>Division</li>
            <li>Department</li>
            <li>Unit</li>
            <li>Team</li>
            <li>Cost Center</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            Cost Center processing also includes the required linkage with Teams.
        </p>

        <p>
            Both active and recently inactive Foundation Object records can be
            processed by the integration.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">04. Secure File Processing</span>

        <h2>SFTP &amp; File Decryption</h2>

        <p>
            SAP CPI receives the organizational data file through SFTP as part
            of a scheduled nightly process.
        </p>

        <p>
            The received file is encrypted, so one of the first processing steps
            in CPI is to decrypt the file before its contents can be validated
            and transformed.
        </p>

        <p>
            Once decrypted, SAP CPI parses the file and extracts the Foundation
            Object records required for processing.
        </p>

        <p>
            Each record contains a <code>DELTA</code> attribute indicating
            whether it should be considered a delta record.
        </p>

        <p>
            The file also contains metadata that can be used for traceability
            and investigation.
        </p>

        <div class="process-flow">
            SFTP → Receive Encrypted File → Decrypt → Parse File → Process Records
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">05. Load Strategy</span>

        <h2>Delta Load &amp; Full Load Processing</h2>

        <p>
            The integration supports two execution modes: Delta Load and Full Load.
        </p>

        <div class="challenge-grid">

            <article>
                <h3>Delta Load</h3>

                <p>
                    During Delta Load processing, SAP CPI reads the complete
                    incoming file but retains only records where
                    <code>DELTA = yes</code>.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Records where <code>DELTA = no</code> are excluded from
                    further delta processing.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The remaining records continue through the validation logic
                    before being sent to SuccessFactors.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>Full Load</h3>

                <p>
                    During Full Load processing, the DELTA filter is bypassed.
                </p>

                <p>
                    SAP CPI processes all records contained in the file,
                    regardless of whether the DELTA attribute is
                    <code>yes</code> or <code>no</code>.
                </p>

                <p>
                    This mode can be used for reconciliation, recovery or
                    complete synchronization scenarios.
                </p>
            </article>

        </div>

        <div class="process-flow">
            Delta Load: File → Filter DELTA = yes → Process Relevant Records
        </div>

        <div class="process-flow">
            Full Load: File → No DELTA Filtering → Process All Records
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">06. Dependency Management</span>

        <h2>Parent-Child Processing Order</h2>

        <p>
            Foundation Objects have dependencies between each other.
        </p>

        <p>
            Some child objects reference parent objects that must already exist
            in SuccessFactors before the dependent records can be successfully
            created or updated.
        </p>

        <p>
            SAP CPI therefore processes the Foundation Objects in a controlled
            sequence.
        </p>

        <p>
            Parent objects are processed before their child objects, ensuring
            that the required references exist before dependent records are sent
            to SuccessFactors.
        </p>

        <p>
            This prevents referential errors and ensures that the organizational
            hierarchy is created in the correct order.
        </p>

        <div class="process-flow">
            Parent Object → Child Object → Dependent Object
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">07. Effective-Dated Processing</span>

        <h2>Foundation Object Version Management</h2>

        <p>
            Foundation Objects in SAP SuccessFactors are effective-dated.
        </p>

        <p>
            SAP CPI handles the effective date information required to create
            the correct organizational versions in Employee Central.
        </p>

        <p>
            The integration also preserves existing end dates where required
            and avoids unintentionally affecting future-dated records already
            present in the system.
        </p>

        <p>
            This helps maintain the consistency of both historical and future
            organizational data.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">08. Execution Reporting</span>

        <h2>Detailed Processing Report</h2>

        <p>
            The integration processes a high volume of Foundation Object records,
            which can make manual investigation difficult.
        </p>

        <p>
            To simplify monitoring and troubleshooting, SAP CPI generates a
            processing report at the end of each execution.
        </p>

        <p>
            The report provides the result of the records processed during the
            integration.
        </p>

        <div class="challenge-grid">

            <article>
                <h3>Successful Processing</h3>

                <p>
                    If all records are processed correctly, the report clearly
                    indicates that the load completed successfully.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>Processing Errors</h3>

                <p>
                    If one or more records fail, the report identifies the
                    affected records and includes the corresponding error details.
                </p>
            </article>

        </div>

        <p>
            This makes it easier to understand the execution result without
            manually investigating a large number of individual transactions.
        </p>

        <div class="process-flow">
            Process Records → Collect Results → Generate Report → Success / Error Details
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="case-study-section">
        <span class="section-number">09. Error Handling</span>

        <h2>Recovery and Reprocessing</h2>

        <p>
            The integration supports reprocessing when errors occur during the
            synchronization.
        </p>

        <p>
            Depending on the issue, the file can be processed again after the
            underlying problem has been corrected.
        </p>

        <p>
            The generated processing report helps identify which records failed
            and why, reducing the time required to investigate and resolve
            processing issues.
        </p>
    </section>


